Further, in the said judgment,
the Co-ordinate Bench referred the judgment of the Hon'ble Apex Court in Mazdoor Kisan Sakti Sangathan Vs. Union of India & another (2018) 17 SCC 324, at paragraph Nos.48 to 68 which reads as follows;
"48.

- 30 - NC: 2026:KHC-K:52 HC-KAR (a) there should not be "unrestricted" holding of public meetings, processions, etc.;
and (b) as a corollary, the order mentions that such public meetings, processions,
demonstrations, etc. would not be allowed "without written permission".
